{"id": "EUVD-2026-58915", "enisaUuid": "0adccceb-8a63-3431-bd14-0917cad196a4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: thunderbolt: Fix frags[] overflow by bounding frame_count\n\ntbnet_poll() assembles a multi-frame ThunderboltIP packet into one skb. The\nfirst frame goes into the skb linear area and every further frame is added as\na page fragment.\n\n\tskb_add_rx_frag(skb, skb_shinfo(skb)->nr_frags,\n\t\t\tpage, hdr_size, frame_size,\n\t\t\tTBNET_RX_PAGE_SIZE - hdr_size);\n\nA packet of frame_count frames therefore ends up with frame_count - 1\nfragments. tbnet_check_frame() only bounds the peer supplied frame_count to\nTBNET_RING_SIZE / 4 (64), which is far above MAX_SKB_FRAGS (17 by default). A\npeer that sends a packet of 19 or more small frames pushes nr_frags past\nMAX_SKB_FRAGS, so skb_add_rx_frag() writes past skb_shinfo()->frags[] and\ncorrupts memory after the shared info.\n\nTighten the start of packet bound to MAX_SKB_FRAGS + 1 so a packet can never\nproduce more fragments than frags[] can hold. This matches the recent skb\nfrags overflow fixes in other receive paths, for example f0813bcd2d9d (\"net:\nwwan: t7xx: fix potential skb->frags overflow in RX path\") and 600dc40554dc\n(\"net: usb: cdc-phonet: fix skb frags[] overflow in rx_complete()\").", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:53:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:44:59", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f96b3b35c622d565eff2438993e028d280163f5c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6262f51e09d8dc8b07599a9e4f03bd3989d13fff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/569ba39b2d12995a29dc158e5b4de6e449278f30", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b3b4e5ff5a58ad32817824b0310e63908b12052", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e27beb4536cbf1d59e2d8c2840e87d972aba906f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e5824d5b841d99a2bcdd4e2c256643293bbc22c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe6b606fbf0c3beb94ccf17fcf31d8c2138264e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/55d9895f89970501fe126d1026b586b04a224c27"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72157", "GHSA-8f5r-c72f-67g5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "093ed67b-04c9-3e84-bc0a-58d988fae09e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.266"}, {"id": "1428e76e-7ee1-37c4-935d-5fa916d333b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.184"}, {"id": "1b9f333d-331e-3425-b0cf-10d69574e474", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e69b6c02b4c3b8d03be7136f90dd9551ad5a5a5e <6262f51e09d8dc8b07599a9e4f03bd3989d13fff"}, {"id": "313415a4-1603-398e-90fd-c81fa3b75fc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.217"}, {"id": "431f6cbd-915b-3ea5-a3a8-f0097d5f786c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e69b6c02b4c3b8d03be7136f90dd9551ad5a5a5e <569ba39b2d12995a29dc158e5b4de6e449278f30"}, {"id": "5a6a7011-10a7-3c19-8a11-6a9d2ecda051", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e69b6c02b4c3b8d03be7136f90dd9551ad5a5a5e <f96b3b35c622d565eff2438993e028d280163f5c"}, {"id": "6ec549b1-aad3-34fe-acb0-200fdcdf3854", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "97a5eeb8-3597-3167-a420-2a127174c5d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e69b6c02b4c3b8d03be7136f90dd9551ad5a5a5e <2b3b4e5ff5a58ad32817824b0310e63908b12052"}, {"id": "9968148b-a4b1-3d88-b809-c646db1a9ca4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e69b6c02b4c3b8d03be7136f90dd9551ad5a5a5e <55d9895f89970501fe126d1026b586b04a224c27"}, {"id": "b3239cde-bb03-34d5-a345-1319e3169c75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "pro